  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "74327d66-caed-4e4e-a51c-4bd3ee8a90a9",
   "metadata": {
    "jp-MarkdownHeadingCollapsed": true,
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "## Measuring the Robustness of K-means Feature Groups [k=3]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "86bb50f3-3226-490f-b402-b2a42546bd20",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This next section is more of a diagnostic test of the robustness of the feature groups. With an independent machine learning algorithm, are the three Feature Groups reproducible? In particular, can a Random Forest Classification model predict the same Feature Group a galaxy that k-means clustering assigned?\n",
    "\n",
    "My approach first involved creating a train (60% of the sample) and test (40% of the sample) set of the same input features as with k-means. I use the same dataframe as the k-means script output, to ensure sample consistency and the ensure I have the column of Feature Clusters. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "4060e988-d501-4700-aa69-8fad535db9d7",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#NO DIFFERENCE BETWEEN SCALED AND UNSCALED PARAMETERS FOR RANDOM FOREST CLASSIFICATION!\n",
    "#output from k-means run is \"df\"\n",
    "\n",
    "#define the x (feature_list) and y (feature_clusters) variable names\n",
    "feature_list = ['CRE_g', 'CRE_r','CRE_W1-fixBA','CRE_W3-fixBA',\n",
    "                  'CN_g', 'CN_r', 'CN_W1-fixBA', 'CN_W3-fixBA']\n",
    "feature_clusters = ['Feature Cluster']\n",
    "\n",
    "#define the actual X and y sets. also include the galaxy IDs for visual inspection later on.\n",
    "#(without VFID, how will I know which galaxy is which?)\n",
    "#also need the PCA components for plotting the clusters...also later on.\n",
    "X = df[feature_list]\n",
    "y = df['Feature Cluster']\n",
    "VFID = df['VFID']\n",
    "pcacomp1, pcacomp2 = df['Comp1'], df['Comp2']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "2b1c0267-8975-4e2d-ab81-7483c0b6a1fa",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#define the training and test sets\n",
    "#I use 60% of the sample for training and 40% for testing\n",
    "#random_state ensures reproducibility. can set to any positive integer.\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test, VFID_train, VFID_test= train_test_split(X, y, VFID,\n",
    "                                                                          test_size=0.4, \n",
    "                                                                          random_state=1, \n",
    "                                                                          stratify=y)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eccc94ea-a799-426a-98d3-0de7ae92ead1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Next, I set up the Random Forest Classification model scaffold with the following hyperparameters: \n",
    "\n",
    "* n_estimators: the number of decision trees used to create the forest \n",
    "* max_depth: dictates maximum complexity (i.e., number of splits) for a decision tree \n",
    "* class_weight: quite simply, how the model weighs each class. 'Balanced' automatically assigns weights to each class inversely proportional to their frequency in the data, ensuring the minority class gets more attention.\n",
    "* max_features: size of the random subsets of features to consider for every decision split (sqrt = sqrt(total number of features) \n",
    "\n",
    "I then fit the model to the training data and use the result to predict the Feature Groups (classes) of the test dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "15e911a8-b652-4f1f-a9ef-49699a13e2e2",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#model scaffold\n",
    "model = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=10, max_depth=14,class_weight='balanced',\n",
    "                               random_state=4,max_features='sqrt')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "a159bfc7-ca2f-4e10-abd9-af14bf06af02",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
